Worse, different proportional fonts are spaced differently, so
proportional ASCII art which looks great in Times on my machine may look
slightly skewed in Times on your machine, and almost certainly will look
decidedly crooked in Helvetica anywhere, and like a dog's dinner in
Courier.
Contrast with non-proportional ASCII art: it may be a bit more elongated
one way or another, but it will at least be the same shape whether you
view it in Courier, Prestige Elite, OCR-B, or a dumb terminal's hardware
font.

